-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- DEDUCTIONS FROM A BENEFIT, AND THE FAMILY ALLOWANCE
-- RECIPIENT (regulations 76, 76.1 and 77).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 747 to 779.
--
-- Regulation 76: recovering a provincial or municipal advance, assistance or welfare payment out of the lump sum a person
-- gets for a period, on the person's irrevocable written consent. Regulation 76.1: paying a disability income program's
-- administrator out of a disability benefit, on the same kind of consent. Regulation 77: who counts as a "family allowance
-- recipient" beyond the Act's own definition (the months of caring for a child under seven drop out of the contributory period).
-- Subsections 76(5) and 77(2) are repealed. A consent is "received before the expiry of one year after the date of their
-- signature": received no later than the same day a year on (fork F-46.2). Money is dollars.

§ `Part V -- Deductions from a benefit, and family allowance recipients (regulations 76 to 77)`

§§ `Regulation 76(1) -- the two definitions`

-- src:747 | 76 (1) In this section,
-- src:748 | authority means any provincial authority or municipal authority in a province that pays any advance or assistance or welfare payment to a person in the province. (autorité)
-- src:749 | excess payment means the amount of any advance or assistance or welfare payment that was paid by an authority to a person for a month or any portion thereof and that would not have been paid if the benefit that was subsequently payable under the Act to that person in respect of that period had in fact been paid during that period. (paiement excédentaire)
@ref Reg 76(1) "authority" (src:748)
GIVEN `the body is a provincial authority or a municipal authority in a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body pays an advance or assistance or welfare payment to a person in the province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(1) — a body is an authority`
    `the body is a provincial authority or a municipal authority in a province`
    `the body pays an advance or assistance or welfare payment to a person in the province` MEANS
    `the body is a provincial authority or a municipal authority in a province`
        AND `the body pays an advance or assistance or welfare payment to a person in the province`

@ref Reg 76(1) "excess payment" (src:749)
GIVEN `the amount was paid by an authority to a person for a month or any portion of a month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount would not have been paid if the benefit subsequently payable under the Act to that person in respect of that period had in fact been paid during that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(1) — an amount is an excess payment`
    `the amount was paid by an authority to a person for a month or any portion of a month`
    `the amount would not have been paid if the benefit subsequently payable under the Act to that person in respect of that period had in fact been paid during that period` MEANS
    `the amount was paid by an authority to a person for a month or any portion of a month`
        AND `the amount would not have been paid if the benefit subsequently payable under the Act to that person in respect of that period had in fact been paid during that period`

§§ `Regulation 76(3), (4) and (6) -- what must be certified, and the conditions of a deduction`

-- src:754 | (3) An authority referred to in subsection (2) shall, before any deduction and payment from a benefit payable under the Act to any person is authorized under subsection (2), certify, in a form satisfactory to the Minister,
-- src:755 | (a) the effective date of commencement and the effective date of termination, if applicable, of the advance or assistance or welfare payment;
-- src:756 | (b) the amount that was paid to the person by the authority for the period during which the excess payment occurred or the amount that the authority applies to have reimbursed, whichever is the lesser; and
-- src:757 | (c) the Social Insurance Number of the contributor as a result of whose participation under the Act the benefit is payable.
@ref Reg 76(3) (src:754-757)
GIVEN `the authority certifies, in a form satisfactory to the Minister, the effective date of commencement and, if applicable, the effective date of termination of the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority certifies the amount paid for the period during which the excess payment occurred, or the amount it applies to have reimbursed, whichever is the lesser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority certifies the Social Insurance Number of the contributor as a result of whose participation under the Act the benefit is payable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(3) — the authority has certified what the regulation requires`
    `the authority certifies, in a form satisfactory to the Minister, the effective date of commencement and, if applicable, the effective date of termination of the payment`
    `the authority certifies the amount paid for the period during which the excess payment occurred, or the amount it applies to have reimbursed, whichever is the lesser`
    `the authority certifies the Social Insurance Number of the contributor as a result of whose participation under the Act the benefit is payable` MEANS
    `the authority certifies, in a form satisfactory to the Minister, the effective date of commencement and, if applicable, the effective date of termination of the payment`
        AND `the authority certifies the amount paid for the period during which the excess payment occurred, or the amount it applies to have reimbursed, whichever is the lesser`
        AND `the authority certifies the Social Insurance Number of the contributor as a result of whose participation under the Act the benefit is payable`

-- src:758 | (4) No deduction and payment in respect of an excess payment shall be authorized pursuant to subsection (2) unless
-- src:759 | (a) the Minister and the appropriate provincial official have concluded an agreement in writing authorizing the deduction and payment;
-- src:760 | (b) the certification required by subsection (3) has been received by the Minister;
-- src:761 | (c) the irrevocable written consent of the person to the deduction and payment by the Minister has been received before the expiry of one year after the date of their signature; and
-- src:762 | (d) the amount of the excess payment is greater than $50.
@ref Reg 76(4)(c) (src:761)
GIVEN `the consent is irrevocable and in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person signed the consent` IS A DATE
      `the date the Minister received the consent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(4)(c) — the irrevocable written consent was received in time`
    `the consent is irrevocable and in writing` `the date the person signed the consent` `the date the Minister received the consent` MEANS
    `the consent is irrevocable and in writing`
        AND `the date the Minister received the consent` AT LEAST `the date the person signed the consent`
        AND `the date the Minister received the consent` AT MOST (`add years` `the date the person signed the consent` 1)

@ref Reg 76(4) (src:758-762)
GIVEN `the Minister and the appropriate provincial official have concluded an agreement in writing authorizing the deduction and payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certification required by subsection (3) has been received by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent is irrevocable and in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person signed the consent` IS A DATE
      `the date the Minister received the consent` IS A DATE
      `the amount of the excess payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(4) — a deduction and payment in respect of an excess payment may be authorized`
    `the Minister and the appropriate provincial official have concluded an agreement in writing authorizing the deduction and payment`
    `the certification required by subsection (3) has been received by the Minister`
    `the consent is irrevocable and in writing`
    `the date the person signed the consent`
    `the date the Minister received the consent`
    `the amount of the excess payment` MEANS
    `the Minister and the appropriate provincial official have concluded an agreement in writing authorizing the deduction and payment`
        AND `the certification required by subsection (3) has been received by the Minister`
        AND `reg 76(4)(c) — the irrevocable written consent was received in time`
              `the consent is irrevocable and in writing` `the date the person signed the consent` `the date the Minister received the consent`
        AND `the amount of the excess payment` GREATER THAN 50

-- src:750 | (2) Subject to subsections (3) to (6), the Minister may, where an authority satisfies him that an excess payment has been paid to a person, authorize
-- src:751 | (a) the deduction from the one sum amount payable to that person in accordance with subsection 62(1) of the Act in respect of the period for which the excess payment was paid, and
-- src:752 | (b) the payment to the provincial authority or municipal authority in the province in which the excess payment was paid,
-- src:753 | of an amount equal to the amount of the excess payment.
@ref Reg 76(2) (src:750-753)
GIVEN `an authority satisfies the Minister that an excess payment has been paid to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a one sum amount is payable to the person in accordance with subsection 62(1) of the Act in respect of the period for which the excess payment was paid` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 62(1) (piece cp5)
      `the Minister and the appropriate provincial official have concluded an agreement in writing authorizing the deduction and payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certification required by subsection (3) has been received by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent is irrevocable and in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person signed the consent` IS A DATE
      `the date the Minister received the consent` IS A DATE
      `the amount of the excess payment` IS A NUMBER
      `a deduction and payment in respect of this excess payment has already been authorized` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76(2) — the amount the Minister may authorize to be deducted and paid`
    `an authority satisfies the Minister that an excess payment has been paid to the person`
    `a one sum amount is payable to the person in accordance with subsection 62(1) of the Act in respect of the period for which the excess payment was paid`
    `the Minister and the appropriate provincial official have concluded an agreement in writing authorizing the deduction and payment`
    `the certification required by subsection (3) has been received by the Minister`
    `the consent is irrevocable and in writing`
    `the date the person signed the consent`
    `the date the Minister received the consent`
    `the amount of the excess payment`
    `a deduction and payment in respect of this excess payment has already been authorized` MEANS
    IF `an authority satisfies the Minister that an excess payment has been paid to the person`
       AND `a one sum amount is payable to the person in accordance with subsection 62(1) of the Act in respect of the period for which the excess payment was paid`
       AND `reg 76(4) — a deduction and payment in respect of an excess payment may be authorized`
              `the Minister and the appropriate provincial official have concluded an agreement in writing authorizing the deduction and payment`
              `the certification required by subsection (3) has been received by the Minister`
              `the consent is irrevocable and in writing`
              `the date the person signed the consent`
              `the date the Minister received the consent`
              `the amount of the excess payment`
       AND (NOT `a deduction and payment in respect of this excess payment has already been authorized`)
    THEN JUST `the amount of the excess payment`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:764 | (6) If, for any reason, no deduction has been made under subsection (2) in respect of an excess payment or a deduction and payment have been made in respect of an excess payment in an amount less than the amount that might have been paid in respect thereof under subsection (2), the Minister shall not authorize the deduction and payment of any other amount in respect of that excess payment.
@ref Reg 76(6) (src:764)
GIVEN `no deduction has been made under subsection (2), or a deduction and payment have been made of less than the amount that might have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(6) — the Minister must not authorize the deduction and payment of any other amount in respect of that excess payment`
    `no deduction has been made under subsection (2), or a deduction and payment have been made of less than the amount that might have been paid` MEANS
    `no deduction has been made under subsection (2), or a deduction and payment have been made of less than the amount that might have been paid`

§§ `Regulation 76.1 -- payment to an administrator of a disability income program`

-- src:767 | 76.1 (1) For the purposes of subsection 65(3) of the Act, the Minister may deduct an amount as described in that subsection from a benefit payable to a person under paragraph 44(1)(b) or (h) of the Act and pay that amount to an administrator approved by the Minister if
-- src:768 | (a) the administrator submits to the Minister a record of the payment made under the disability income program, together with the person’s irrevocable written consent to the deduction and payment;
-- src:769 | (b) the documents referred to in paragraph (a) are received by the Minister within one year after the date on which the consent is signed; and
-- src:770 | (c) the amount exceeds $50.
-- src:771 | (2) For the purpose of subsection 65(3) of the Act, if, for any reason, no deduction has been made or a deduction and payment have been made by the Minister for an amount that is less than the amount that might have been paid under that subsection, the Minister shall not authorize any other deduction and payment.
@ref Reg 76.1(1) (src:767-770)
GIVEN `the benefit payable` IS A `Kind of benefit`
      `the amount is one described in subsection 65(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 65(3) (piece cp4)
      `the administrator is approved by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the administrator submits a record of the payment made under the disability income program together with the person's irrevocable written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person signed the consent` IS A DATE
      `the date the Minister receives the documents` IS A DATE
      `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76.1(1) — the Minister may deduct an amount from a benefit and pay it to an administrator`
    `the benefit payable`
    `the amount is one described in subsection 65(3) of the Act`
    `the administrator is approved by the Minister`
    `the administrator submits a record of the payment made under the disability income program together with the person's irrevocable written consent`
    `the date the person signed the consent`
    `the date the Minister receives the documents`
    `the amount` MEANS
    (    `the benefit payable` EQUALS `a disability pension`
      OR `the benefit payable` EQUALS `a post-retirement disability benefit`)
        AND `the amount is one described in subsection 65(3) of the Act`
        AND `the administrator is approved by the Minister`
        AND `the administrator submits a record of the payment made under the disability income program together with the person's irrevocable written consent`
        AND `the date the Minister receives the documents` AT LEAST `the date the person signed the consent`
        AND `the date the Minister receives the documents` AT MOST (`add years` `the date the person signed the consent` 1)
        AND `the amount` GREATER THAN 50

@ref Reg 76.1(2) (src:771)
GIVEN `no deduction has been made, or a deduction and payment have been made of less than the amount that might have been paid under subsection 65(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76.1(2) — the Minister must not authorize any other deduction and payment`
    `no deduction has been made, or a deduction and payment have been made of less than the amount that might have been paid under subsection 65(3) of the Act` MEANS
    `no deduction has been made, or a deduction and payment have been made of less than the amount that might have been paid under subsection 65(3) of the Act`

§§ `Regulation 77 -- family allowance recipient`

-- Paragraph (a): the allowance period is "before the child reached the age of seven"; the child reaches seven on the date
-- section 2(2) of the Act deems (regulation 77 is not among the provisions section 2(2) excepts): the first day of the month
-- after the seventh birthday's month. Paragraphs (b) to (d) say "a child under seven" and are states, tested as facts.
-- src:774 | 77 (1) For the purposes of the definition family allowance recipient in subsection 42(1) of the Act, family allowance recipient includes
-- src:775 | (a) the spouse, former spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner of a person who is described in that definition as having received or being in receipt of an allowance or a family allowance in respect of a child for any period before the child reached the age of seven, if that spouse, former spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner remained at home during that period as the child’s primary caregiver and that period has not already been or cannot be excluded or deducted from the person’s contributory period under Part II of the Act;
-- src:776 | (b) a member of the Canadian Armed Forces who, before 1973, was posted to serve outside Canada, or the spouse or former spouse of such a member, who, but for the posting, would have received an allowance or family allowance for a child under seven years of age;
-- src:777 | (c) the person who, under section 122.62 of the Income Tax Act, is considered to be an eligible individual for the purposes of subdivision a.1 of Division E of Part I of that Act (Canada child benefit) in respect of a qualified dependant under seven years of age; and
-- src:778 | (d) the person who would have been considered to be an eligible individual for the purposes of subdivision a.1 of Division E of Part I of the Income Tax Act (Canada child benefit) had a notice been filed under subsection 122.62(1) of that Act, where no person was considered to be an eligible individual in respect of the same qualified dependant under seven years of age.
@ref Reg 77(1) (src:774-778)
GIVEN `the person is described in the definition family allowance recipient in subsection 42(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 42(1) (piece cp3)
      `the person is the spouse, former spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner of a person described in that definition as having received an allowance or a family allowance in respect of a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period for which the allowance was received` IS A DATE
      `the person remained at home during that period as the child's primary caregiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that period has already been excluded or deducted from the person's contributory period under Part II of the Act, or can be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the Canadian Armed Forces who before 1973 was posted to serve outside Canada, or the spouse or former spouse of such a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for the posting the person would have received an allowance or family allowance for a child under seven years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is considered under section 122.62 of the Income Tax Act to be an eligible individual in respect of a qualified dependant under seven years of age` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the Income Tax Act is not deposited
      `the person would have been considered an eligible individual in respect of a qualified dependant under seven years of age had a notice been filed under subsection 122.62(1) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no person was considered to be an eligible individual in respect of the same qualified dependant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 77(1) — a person is a family allowance recipient for the purposes of the Act`
    `the person is described in the definition family allowance recipient in subsection 42(1) of the Act`
    `the person is the spouse, former spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner of a person described in that definition as having received an allowance or a family allowance in respect of a child`
    `the child's date of birth`
    `the last day of the period for which the allowance was received`
    `the person remained at home during that period as the child's primary caregiver`
    `that period has already been excluded or deducted from the person's contributory period under Part II of the Act, or can be`
    `the person is a member of the Canadian Armed Forces who before 1973 was posted to serve outside Canada, or the spouse or former spouse of such a member`
    `but for the posting the person would have received an allowance or family allowance for a child under seven years of age`
    `the person is considered under section 122.62 of the Income Tax Act to be an eligible individual in respect of a qualified dependant under seven years of age`
    `the person would have been considered an eligible individual in respect of a qualified dependant under seven years of age had a notice been filed under subsection 122.62(1) of that Act`
    `no person was considered to be an eligible individual in respect of the same qualified dependant` MEANS
    `the person is described in the definition family allowance recipient in subsection 42(1) of the Act`
        OR (    `the person is the spouse, former spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner of a person described in that definition as having received an allowance or a family allowance in respect of a child`
            AND `the last day of the period for which the allowance was received` LESS THAN
                (`s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `any other provision` `the child's date of birth` 7)
            AND `the person remained at home during that period as the child's primary caregiver`
            AND (NOT `that period has already been excluded or deducted from the person's contributory period under Part II of the Act, or can be`))
        OR (    `the person is a member of the Canadian Armed Forces who before 1973 was posted to serve outside Canada, or the spouse or former spouse of such a member`
            AND `but for the posting the person would have received an allowance or family allowance for a child under seven years of age`)
        OR `the person is considered under section 122.62 of the Income Tax Act to be an eligible individual in respect of a qualified dependant under seven years of age`
        OR (    `the person would have been considered an eligible individual in respect of a qualified dependant under seven years of age had a notice been filed under subsection 122.62(1) of that Act`
            AND `no person was considered to be an eligible individual in respect of the same qualified dependant`)
